  "query_preview": "../Monday through Thursday/...The week starts out warm\nwith the chance for seasonably higher temperatures across the \nsouthern panhandle. Mid to high 70s are likely, with guidance \nindicating Hyder as the warmest location. With guidance continuing\nto indicate a set up favorable for warm temperatures, it will \nlikely come down to local effects from a marine layer and cloud \ncover to downsloping and wind speeds. Wednesday looks to be warm \nas well, but high temps are expected to be in the lower 70s. \nThrough the start of the week, no rain is expected except for \nalong the NE gulf coast overnight Monday into Tuesday as a week \nfront breaks apart across the area. Thursday then brings the \nchance for rain back into the equation for the northern panhandle \nas an area of low pressure moves across the northern gulf.",
